  "title": "Su Song's astronomical clock tower",
  "summary": "In 1088 Su Song built a water-powered astronomical clock tower in the Song capital Bianjing, now Kaifeng. An armillary sphere stood on top, a celestial globe in the middle and wooden figures striking the time below. The Science Museum Group notes its waterwheel acted as an escapement. His son Su Xie later failed to rebuild it.",
